; One miner. Local metres, root at the feet, facing -Z (Vector3.FORWARD).
;
; The art is authored facing +Z, which is this project's convention backwards.
; The 180 degree yaw that corrects it lives on Rig, not on the three placements
; in the level and not in the model - reversing the art would silently turn the
; character around in every other scene that already places it.
;
; The blend tree is two layers: idle_float everywhere, and a single held
; helmet-gesture pose filtered onto the right arm alone. The cutscene keys
; blend_amount rather than the bones, so only one mixer ever writes this
; skeleton - and because the layer is a held pose rather than a clip, that one
; weight is the whole gesture and it scrubs with the timeline like every other
; track. See miner_rig.gd and build_elevator_intro_animation.gd.

